WEBVTT

00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:12.987
Personal Log, Stardate 47391.2.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.864
I am returning from the bat'leth
competition on Forcas III.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.198
The conditions were difficult.

00:00:19.236 --> 00:00:24.071
Several contestants were maimed,
but I was triumphant.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:29.238
I won Champion Standing.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:33.648
I am looking forward to resuming
my duties aboard the Enterprise.

00:00:33.684 --> 00:00:37.643
However, I am anticipating
a troubling situation.

00:00:42.192 --> 00:00:43.921
It looks like we're going
to have to head

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:45.155
into the Argus Array.

00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:48.164
This is the third time this year
it's stopped relaying data.

00:00:48.198 --> 00:00:49.688
Starfleet's beginning to think

00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:51.758
that it's more
than a simple malfunction.

00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:55.636
I want you to start
a long-range scan once we get...

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.939
Lieutenant,
are you listening to me?

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:02.241
Hmm? Yes, sir.

00:01:04.414 --> 00:01:05.506
You seem awfully tense

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:07.710
for a man who just came back
from vacation.

00:01:07.751 --> 00:01:12.882
Today is my... birthday.

00:01:28.438 --> 00:01:30.838
What's the matter with you?

00:01:30.874 --> 00:01:34.105
Because it is my birthday

00:01:34.144 --> 00:01:36.669
I assumed that you
or one of the others

00:01:36.713 --> 00:01:40.240
would try to mount
an unexpected social gathering.

00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:42.183
A surprise party?

00:01:42.219 --> 00:01:44.380
Mr. Worf, I hate
surprise parties.

00:01:44.421 --> 00:01:46.252
I would never do that to you.

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:48.416
I am sorry, Commander.

00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:49.425
Settle in.

00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:50.426
I'll meet you on the Bridge.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.654
Aye, sir.

00:02:07.077 --> 00:02:08.408
Surprise!

00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:19.784
I love surprise parties.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.723
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:54.758 --> 00:02:58.592
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:58.628 --> 00:03:00.596
Its continuing mission...

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:04.498
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:08.971
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:09.005 --> 00:03:13.567
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:14.362
? Cha Worf Toh'gah-nah
Io Pre'tOk?

00:04:14.404 --> 00:04:15.962
? Cha Worf
Toh'gah-nah Io Pre'tOk?

00:04:16.006 --> 00:04:20.602
? Cha Worf Toh'gah-nah
Io Pre'tOk?

00:04:20.644 --> 00:04:24.444
? Tu Mak Dagh Cha doh Borak!?

00:04:28.084 --> 00:04:30.109
That was not a Klingon song.

00:04:30.153 --> 00:04:32.053
It wasn't easy to translate.

00:04:32.088 --> 00:04:35.114
There doesn't seem to be
a Klingon word for "jolly."

00:04:35.158 --> 00:04:37.991
It's traditional
for the birthday boy

00:04:38.028 --> 00:04:39.620
to cut the cake.

00:04:39.663 --> 00:04:42.757
Captain Picard sends
his birthday wishes.

00:04:42.799 --> 00:04:44.266
He was needed on the Bridge.

00:04:55.178 --> 00:04:56.702
Happy birthday, Worf.

00:04:56.746 --> 00:04:59.306
Thank you.

00:05:04.854 --> 00:05:06.344
Ah...

00:05:08.158 --> 00:05:09.591
a painting.

00:05:09.626 --> 00:05:12.254
Yes. I have entered
my Expressionist phase.

00:05:12.295 --> 00:05:16.288
This is my interpretation
of the Battle of HarOs.

00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:18.699
The Battle of HarOs.

00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:20.999
I think it's wonderful

00:05:21.037 --> 00:05:23.665
and I know just where to put it.

00:05:23.707 --> 00:05:24.765
What are you doing?

00:05:24.808 --> 00:05:28.141
I always thought
this room could use

00:05:28.178 --> 00:05:29.975
a little more color.

00:05:31.915 --> 00:05:32.882
Nice.

00:05:32.983 --> 00:05:35.417
The Battle of HarOs, right?

00:05:37.487 --> 00:05:39.887
Worf, are you all right?

00:05:39.956 --> 00:05:43.414
Yes... yes, I think
Data's painting

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.984
is making me dizzy.

00:05:45.028 --> 00:05:46.518
Some cake.

00:05:46.563 --> 00:05:48.463
Oh, thank you, Doctor.

00:05:48.498 --> 00:05:50.989
I... I thought
the cake was chocolate.

00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:52.092
Don't I wish.

00:05:52.135 --> 00:05:53.625
This is from Alexander.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.900
He gave it to me
just before he left

00:05:56.006 --> 00:05:57.439
to visit your parents.

00:05:57.474 --> 00:05:58.634
Thank you.

00:06:02.312 --> 00:06:03.973
What is it, Worf?

00:06:04.014 --> 00:06:07.780
It's a cast
of Alexander's forehead...

00:06:07.817 --> 00:06:09.284
the ridges of a warrior.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:10.786
He wished he could

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.118
have been here when you got back
from shore leave.

00:06:13.156 --> 00:06:14.555
You should have seen him, Worf.

00:06:14.591 --> 00:06:15.580
He stayed up all night

00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:18.219
talking about how proud he was
of his father.

00:06:18.261 --> 00:06:20.957
Thank you for watching him
while I was away.

00:06:20.997 --> 00:06:22.658
Oh, it was my pleasure.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:25.827
So, how old are you, Mr. Worf?

00:06:25.869 --> 00:06:29.032
Captain... I was told
you could not attend.

00:06:29.072 --> 00:06:31.973
I wouldn't miss this
for the world.

00:06:32.008 --> 00:06:33.373
How old are you?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.503
I am...

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.048
old enough.

00:06:48.425 --> 00:06:49.551
Report.

00:06:49.592 --> 00:06:50.889
The Array appears

00:06:50.927 --> 00:06:52.394
to be functioning normally, sir.

00:06:52.429 --> 00:06:53.396
That can't be right.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.897
We were told the Array

00:06:54.931 --> 00:06:57.263
stopped relaying data
six days ago.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:58.892
The Array is still
transmitting data, sir

00:06:58.935 --> 00:07:01.403
but it is no longer sending that
information to the Federation.

00:07:01.438 --> 00:07:06.501
It appears someone has
redirected its imaging systems.

00:07:06.543 --> 00:07:09.034
Where is the information
being sent now?

00:07:09.079 --> 00:07:10.706
Sector 19658, sir.

00:07:10.747 --> 00:07:13.238
I am unable to access
its main computer

00:07:13.283 --> 00:07:17.117
so it is impossible to determine
its exact location.

00:07:17.153 --> 00:07:18.711
What's in that sector?

00:07:18.755 --> 00:07:19.847
It is uninhabited

00:07:19.923 --> 00:07:21.584
but there could be a ship

00:07:21.624 --> 00:07:24.718
or a subspace relay station
receiving the data.

00:07:24.761 --> 00:07:27.855
Captain, I suggest we beam
a repair team aboard the Array.

00:07:27.897 --> 00:07:30.024
We can begin downloading
their imaging logs

00:07:30.066 --> 00:07:32.296
find out
what the Array's been observing

00:07:32.335 --> 00:07:33.825
for the past six days.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.837
Make it so.

00:07:34.871 --> 00:07:36.065
Mr. Data?

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.285
Excuse me, Counselor.

00:07:52.322 --> 00:07:53.687
Do you have a moment?

00:07:53.723 --> 00:07:55.156
Of course.

00:07:58.228 --> 00:08:01.322
I have been meaning to speak
with you about Alexander.

00:08:01.364 --> 00:08:03.264
Oh?

00:08:03.299 --> 00:08:06.962
It has never been easy for me
having Alexander on board.

00:08:07.003 --> 00:08:10.461
I have tried to be a good
father, to give him guidance

00:08:10.507 --> 00:08:13.840
but he seems to have
his own mind about some things.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.707
Most children do.

00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:19.112
I could not have come this far
without your help

00:08:19.149 --> 00:08:21.310
and Alexander looks up to you.

00:08:21.351 --> 00:08:25.310
At times, I have felt that you
were like a mother to him.

00:08:25.355 --> 00:08:27.550
Worf, that's one
of the nicest things

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:29.148
anyone's ever said to me.

00:08:29.192 --> 00:08:33.185
One time when I thought
I was going to die

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:36.665
I asked you
to watch over Alexander.

00:08:36.699 --> 00:08:39.600
I was wondering
if you would consider

00:08:39.636 --> 00:08:41.968
formalizing that arrangement.

00:08:42.005 --> 00:08:46.442
I want you to be
Alexander's Soh-chlm.

00:08:46.476 --> 00:08:50.207
His... Soh-chlm?

00:08:50.246 --> 00:08:52.771
You would become
his surrogate mother.

00:08:52.816 --> 00:08:55.046
In case anything
ever happened to me

00:08:55.084 --> 00:08:57.177
you would be
responsible for him.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.485
I don't know what to say.

00:09:01.558 --> 00:09:03.389
It's a great honor.

00:09:05.361 --> 00:09:09.525
So, um, that would make me
your...

00:09:09.566 --> 00:09:12.399
The closest analogy is...

00:09:12.435 --> 00:09:13.732
stepsister.

00:09:16.539 --> 00:09:20.373
That would make my mother
your stepmother.

00:09:22.712 --> 00:09:24.680
I had not considered that.

00:09:28.885 --> 00:09:31.183
It is a risk
I am willing to take.

00:09:31.221 --> 00:09:34.019
I accept.

00:09:34.057 --> 00:09:37.686
Lieutenant Worf,
please report to Engineering.

00:09:37.727 --> 00:09:39.217
I am on my way.

00:09:46.069 --> 00:09:48.264
We have analyzed
the imaging logs.

00:09:48.304 --> 00:09:51.239
It appears the Array
was reprogrammed

00:09:51.274 --> 00:09:54.175
to observe several
Federation sites.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:57.304
This is Deep Space 5,
Starbase 47

00:09:57.347 --> 00:10:00.976
the ladara Colony and
the Utopia Planitia Shipyards.

00:10:01.017 --> 00:10:04.111
They're responsible
for new starship development.

00:10:04.153 --> 00:10:06.178
Someone is using the Array

00:10:06.222 --> 00:10:09.089
for covert surveillance
of the Federation.

00:10:09.125 --> 00:10:10.422
That is our theory.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:13.520
We believe unauthorized access
was made six days ago.

00:10:13.563 --> 00:10:15.326
The imaging logs from that day

00:10:15.365 --> 00:10:18.300
show a ship
approaching the Array.

00:10:18.334 --> 00:10:20.825
That is a Cardassian ship,
Galor-class.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.895
We're only three light-years
from Cardassian space.

00:10:23.006 --> 00:10:24.735
They would have easy access
to the Array.

00:10:24.774 --> 00:10:27.208
Mr. Worf, start
a long-range scan of the region.

00:10:27.243 --> 00:10:29.302
See if there are
any Cardassian ships nearby.

00:10:29.345 --> 00:10:30.437
Aye, sir.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.074
Worf, here's
a propulsion analysis

00:10:33.116 --> 00:10:34.674
of the Cardassian vessel.

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:36.617
You might try scanning
for its energy configuration.

00:10:36.653 --> 00:10:38.951
Lieutenant, are you all right?

00:10:41.991 --> 00:10:43.788
I feel dizzy.

00:10:50.199 --> 00:10:53.225
Worf, you don't look so good.

00:10:53.269 --> 00:10:55.601
Maybe you ought
to go to Sick Bay.

00:10:55.638 --> 00:10:58.937
Yes... yes, perhaps I will.

00:11:08.883 --> 00:11:11.852
Any nausea or blurred vision?

00:11:13.321 --> 00:11:14.447
No.

00:11:14.489 --> 00:11:16.684
However, I did experience

00:11:16.724 --> 00:11:20.592
some dizziness earlier today
at my birthday celebration.

00:11:20.628 --> 00:11:22.653
Sounds like you're having
some of the side effects

00:11:22.697 --> 00:11:23.925
from the concussion.

00:11:23.998 --> 00:11:26.899
I can give you some vertazine
for the dizziness

00:11:26.935 --> 00:11:28.596
but I'd like you to rest.

00:11:28.636 --> 00:11:31.935
Doctor, perhaps you are thinking
of another patient.

00:11:31.973 --> 00:11:33.338
I have no concussion.

00:11:33.374 --> 00:11:35.934
Worf, you came in here
this morning

00:11:35.977 --> 00:11:38.605
complaining of ringing
in your ears.

00:11:38.646 --> 00:11:41.376
I scanned you.
You had a concussion.

00:11:41.416 --> 00:11:44.044
You don't remember any of this.

00:11:44.085 --> 00:11:45.814
No.

00:11:45.853 --> 00:11:47.480
Temporary memory loss

00:11:47.522 --> 00:11:50.184
is common
for this kind of injury.

00:11:50.224 --> 00:11:53.853
Do you remember telling me
about the bat'leth tournament?

00:11:53.895 --> 00:11:56.125
You said that one
of the competitors

00:11:56.164 --> 00:11:57.597
hit you over the head.

00:11:57.632 --> 00:12:00.157
That's why you lost the match.

00:12:00.201 --> 00:12:05.070
I won that tournament,
and I can prove it to you!

00:12:18.052 --> 00:12:20.384
What's wrong?

00:12:20.421 --> 00:12:22.719
It says "ninth place."

00:12:28.129 --> 00:12:31.223
This is not the same trophy.

00:12:31.265 --> 00:12:33.927
Someone is playing
a trick on me.

00:12:33.968 --> 00:12:35.401
Worf, try to stay calm.

00:12:35.436 --> 00:12:37.802
Memory loss can be
very disorienting.

00:12:37.839 --> 00:12:39.830
The log...

00:12:39.874 --> 00:12:41.364
I recorded a personal log

00:12:41.409 --> 00:12:43.400
on my way back
to the Enterprise.

00:12:44.645 --> 00:12:50.049
Computer, access personal logs
on Shuttlecraft Curie.

00:12:50.084 --> 00:12:54.043
Show my log entry
for Stardate 47391.2.

00:12:54.088 --> 00:12:58.286
Personal Log, Stardate 47391.2.

00:12:58.326 --> 00:13:01.989
I am returning from the bat'leth
competition on Forcas III.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:04.692
The conditions were difficult.

00:13:04.732 --> 00:13:06.893
Several contenders were maimed.

00:13:06.934 --> 00:13:10.631
One of the contenders used
an illegal T'gha maneuver on me.

00:13:10.671 --> 00:13:14.266
The judges chose to ignore it

00:13:14.308 --> 00:13:17.903
and I was robbed
of my rightful standing.

00:13:17.979 --> 00:13:19.446
I was awarded ninth place.

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.778
I am looking forward

00:13:21.816 --> 00:13:23.807
to resuming my duties
aboard the En...

00:13:28.589 --> 00:13:31.922
I do not understand.

00:13:31.959 --> 00:13:35.622
Worf, I'm sure this is
very disturbing for you

00:13:35.663 --> 00:13:36.925
but don't worry.

00:13:36.998 --> 00:13:39.023
Your memories will return.

00:13:39.067 --> 00:13:41.627
Now, the best thing you
could do right now

00:13:41.669 --> 00:13:44.331
is to settle back into
your normal routine...

00:13:44.372 --> 00:13:45.930
but slowly.

00:13:47.875 --> 00:13:50.241
Thank you, Doctor.

00:13:50.278 --> 00:13:51.768
Let me know if you have

00:13:51.813 --> 00:13:54.043
any more problems
with dizziness.

00:13:54.082 --> 00:13:55.879
I'll give you a hypospray.

00:14:11.899 --> 00:14:13.526
Lieutenant...

00:14:13.568 --> 00:14:14.762
have you completed

00:14:14.802 --> 00:14:17.236
the metallurgical scan
of the Array?

00:14:17.271 --> 00:14:18.465
Sir?

00:14:18.506 --> 00:14:20.133
The metallurgical scan.

00:14:20.174 --> 00:14:21.732
Have you completed it?

00:14:21.776 --> 00:14:24.176
I do not remember
you asking me...

00:14:24.212 --> 00:14:27.670
Captain, there's
a Cardassian ship approaching...

00:14:27.715 --> 00:14:29.342
Galor-class.

00:14:29.383 --> 00:14:30.645
Open a channel.

00:14:30.685 --> 00:14:32.209
On screen.

00:14:32.253 --> 00:14:35.916
This is Captain Jean-Luc Picard
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:37.924
You are in Federation territory.

00:14:38.025 --> 00:14:39.890
Please explain your presence.

00:14:39.927 --> 00:14:41.394
We were wondering

00:14:41.429 --> 00:14:44.330
the same thing about you,
Captain.

00:14:44.365 --> 00:14:48.893
Why would Starfleet's flagship
want to venture so close

00:14:48.936 --> 00:14:51.268
to the Cardassian border?

00:14:51.305 --> 00:14:54.672
We are repairing
one of our subspace telescopes.

00:14:54.709 --> 00:14:57.644
I see.

00:14:57.678 --> 00:14:59.942
May we offer our assistance?

00:15:00.014 --> 00:15:01.276
No, thank you.

00:15:01.315 --> 00:15:03.510
Everything is under control.

00:15:03.551 --> 00:15:05.280
If you don't mind my asking

00:15:05.319 --> 00:15:10.689
what exactly is this telescope
of yours designed to do?

00:15:10.725 --> 00:15:13.125
It is a long-range
subspace array.

00:15:13.161 --> 00:15:16.255
We use it for gathering data
on astronomical phenomena.

00:15:16.297 --> 00:15:19.027
I'm certain
it would never be used

00:15:19.066 --> 00:15:21.762
to observe
a neighboring species.

00:15:21.802 --> 00:15:23.463
Certainly not.

00:15:23.504 --> 00:15:27.531
Well, then,
best of luck with your repairs.

00:15:27.575 --> 00:15:29.702
Just try to make certain

00:15:29.744 --> 00:15:34.738
that your studies are limited
to astronomical phenomena.

00:15:35.616 --> 00:15:37.743
Charming fellow.

00:15:37.785 --> 00:15:40.413
Captain, that ship
was responsible

00:15:40.454 --> 00:15:42.547
for reprogramming the Array.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.148
What are you saying?

00:15:44.192 --> 00:15:47.059
It is the same class
and energy configuration

00:15:47.094 --> 00:15:49.858
as the ship we saw
in the imaging logs.

00:15:49.897 --> 00:15:51.865
The imaging logs?

00:15:51.899 --> 00:15:54.527
Are you suggesting
that you have evidence

00:15:54.569 --> 00:15:57.800
that the Cardassians
have tampered with the Array?

00:15:57.838 --> 00:16:00.329
They are using the Array
as a surveillance device.

00:16:00.374 --> 00:16:01.807
You saw the logs yourself.

00:16:03.177 --> 00:16:05.543
I haven't heard anything
about this.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:06.774
Neither have I.

00:16:06.814 --> 00:16:09.408
Commander Data,
show them the logs

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.884
you downloaded from the Array.

00:16:11.986 --> 00:16:15.012
I know of no such logs.

00:16:16.724 --> 00:16:18.248
Mr. Worf, are you feeling
all right?

00:16:18.292 --> 00:16:19.589
Yes.

00:16:19.627 --> 00:16:23.222
Mr. Data, perhaps you
had better reexamine the Array.

00:16:23.264 --> 00:16:28.429
See if you can find any evidence
to support Mr. Worf's claims.

00:16:31.639 --> 00:16:35.405
Dr. Crusher says I am
experiencing further memory loss

00:16:35.443 --> 00:16:37.468
but my instincts tell me
it is more than that.

00:16:37.511 --> 00:16:38.808
I remember those imaging logs.

00:16:38.846 --> 00:16:40.711
I could tell you
every detail, every word!

00:16:40.748 --> 00:16:43.308
Worf, let's assume
for a second you're right...

00:16:43.351 --> 00:16:46.843
that things did happen
as you remember them.

00:16:46.887 --> 00:16:49.651
Are you saying that everyone's
memory on this ship

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.487
has been altered but yours?

00:16:52.827 --> 00:16:54.158
Enter.

00:16:57.131 --> 00:16:58.428
Counselor.

00:16:58.466 --> 00:17:00.058
Worf, I wanted you to know

00:17:00.101 --> 00:17:02.331
that we reexamined
the imaging logs.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.531
They don't show
a Cardassian ship

00:17:04.572 --> 00:17:07.973
or any evidence that the Array
was reprogrammed.

00:17:08.009 --> 00:17:09.374
From what we can tell

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.504
the Array suffered
a simple mechanical failure.

00:17:12.546 --> 00:17:14.104
That is not right!

00:17:14.148 --> 00:17:16.013
I was certain that...

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.415
What's wrong?

00:17:32.433 --> 00:17:36.870
Counselor, the painting
that Commander Data gave me...

00:17:36.904 --> 00:17:38.599
it has moved.

00:17:38.639 --> 00:17:40.834
Worf, I hung that painting
there...

00:17:40.875 --> 00:17:43.105
at your birthday party,
remember?

00:17:43.144 --> 00:17:46.375
No...

00:17:46.414 --> 00:17:48.609
The painting has changed.

00:17:48.649 --> 00:17:51.641
Don't you see it?

00:17:51.686 --> 00:17:53.881
Your hair, and your clothing...

00:17:53.921 --> 00:17:56.583
they have changed as well!

00:17:56.624 --> 00:18:00.560
Worf, maybe you should come
with me to Sick Bay and...

00:18:00.594 --> 00:18:01.993
Now, Mr. Worf.

00:18:05.132 --> 00:18:07.123
Now!

00:18:18.813 --> 00:18:21.281
What are you waiting for?!
Raise the shields!

00:18:21.315 --> 00:18:24.546
This panel configuration
has been altered.

00:18:24.585 --> 00:18:26.177
I do not know how...

00:18:27.588 --> 00:18:30.455
Direct hit, Engineering section
and deck 42.

00:18:30.491 --> 00:18:32.721
Shield generators
are overloading.

00:18:34.929 --> 00:18:36.726
Number One.

00:18:39.633 --> 00:18:41.999
Firing photon torpedoes.

00:18:42.036 --> 00:18:43.367
Full spread.

00:18:48.409 --> 00:18:50.502
Direct hit
on their main reactor.

00:18:50.544 --> 00:18:52.068
They're returning fire.

00:18:52.113 --> 00:18:54.047
Captain, we have sustained

00:18:54.081 --> 00:18:57.539
heavy damage
to the deflector systems.

00:18:57.585 --> 00:18:59.382
Hull breaches
on decks 17 and 36.

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:01.718
Ensign, take us out of here.
Maximum warp.

00:19:01.756 --> 00:19:03.553
Aye, sir.

00:19:03.591 --> 00:19:05.149
Are they pursuing us?

00:19:05.192 --> 00:19:06.420
No, sir.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:09.190
They are firing
on the Argus Array.

00:19:10.798 --> 00:19:13.289
They destroyed it, sir.

00:19:15.035 --> 00:19:16.400
Bridge to Engineering.

00:19:16.437 --> 00:19:17.870
Mr. La Forge,
what's your status?

00:19:17.905 --> 00:19:19.372
This is Ensign Hayes, sir.

00:19:19.407 --> 00:19:21.272
Commander La Forge
has been taken to Sick Bay

00:19:21.308 --> 00:19:23.469
with plasma burns.

00:19:23.511 --> 00:19:26.708
There's serious damage
to the secondary plasma conduit

00:19:26.747 --> 00:19:28.112
but I think we've got it
under control.

00:19:28.149 --> 00:19:29.275
Acknowledged.

00:19:29.316 --> 00:19:32.251
Ensign, lay in a course
to Starbase 129.

00:19:32.286 --> 00:19:34.277
Aye, sir.

00:19:34.321 --> 00:19:37.848
What happened back there,
Mr. Worf?

00:19:37.892 --> 00:19:42.522
I believe I experienced
another memory loss.

00:19:42.563 --> 00:19:43.655
Memory loss?

00:19:43.697 --> 00:19:45.688
What are you talking about?

00:19:45.733 --> 00:19:49.066
I do not feel well.

00:19:49.103 --> 00:19:50.331
Request permission

00:19:50.371 --> 00:19:53.169
to be temporarily
relieved of duty, sir.

00:19:53.207 --> 00:19:54.196
Granted.

00:20:28.175 --> 00:20:32.737
Computer, access personal logs
on Shuttlecraft Curie.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:35.874
Play log entry
for Stardate 47391.2.

00:20:35.916 --> 00:20:37.110
There is no log entry

00:20:37.151 --> 00:20:39.881
from the Shuttlecraft Curie
for that stardate.

00:20:41.288 --> 00:20:43.950
Computer,
display any log entries

00:20:43.991 --> 00:20:48.325
concerning the bat'leth
tournament on Forcas III.

00:20:48.362 --> 00:20:52.662
Personal Log, Stardate 47391.2.

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:55.965
There has been a malfunction
in the ship's main deflector.

00:20:56.003 --> 00:20:59.063
It will require
two more days of repairs.

00:20:59.106 --> 00:21:02.075
As a result,
I will not be able to compete

00:21:02.109 --> 00:21:04.441
in the bat'leth tournament
on Forcas III.

00:21:04.478 --> 00:21:07.777
I have asked my brother
to take my place.

00:21:07.815 --> 00:21:10.443
He does not have my prowess
with the blade, but...

00:21:24.764 --> 00:21:26.732
Why did you lock the door?

00:21:26.766 --> 00:21:28.495
Why shouldn't I?

00:21:28.534 --> 00:21:30.934
I heard what happened
on the Bridge.

00:21:31.003 --> 00:21:32.664
Are you all right?

00:21:34.407 --> 00:21:36.272
I am not sure.

00:21:36.309 --> 00:21:37.708
Do you want to talk about it?

00:21:37.743 --> 00:21:39.404
I would rather not, Counselor.

00:21:39.445 --> 00:21:43.313
Very well... Lieutenant.

00:21:44.884 --> 00:21:46.784
Hot chocolate.

00:21:48.221 --> 00:21:51.190
Is there something
I can do for you?

00:21:51.224 --> 00:21:54.193
Actually, there is.

00:22:14.814 --> 00:22:16.611
Come and sit down.

00:22:25.658 --> 00:22:29.389
I just want you
to relax for a minute.

00:22:32.765 --> 00:22:34.323
There.

00:22:44.744 --> 00:22:48.009
You are so tense.

00:22:49.849 --> 00:22:52.249
Now, I know you
don't want to talk

00:22:52.285 --> 00:22:54.617
about what happened
on the Bridge

00:22:54.654 --> 00:22:55.951
but there are times

00:22:56.055 --> 00:22:58.819
when it's just best
to let things out.

00:23:00.593 --> 00:23:02.618
Come on.

00:23:02.662 --> 00:23:07.065
If you can't talk to me,
who can you talk to, hmm?

00:23:07.099 --> 00:23:09.124
Aw!

00:23:09.168 --> 00:23:11.898
I do not believe
this is appropriate behavior.

00:23:11.938 --> 00:23:13.633
Even for your wife?

00:23:13.673 --> 00:23:16.005
Wife?!

00:23:21.414 --> 00:23:24.383
Worf, what's wrong?

00:23:24.417 --> 00:23:26.612
I do not know.

00:23:26.652 --> 00:23:29.450
Things are changing.

00:23:29.488 --> 00:23:31.752
What's changed?

00:23:34.093 --> 00:23:38.189
I do not remember us...
you and I... being mates.

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:41.358
It is as if events
and circumstances

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:44.301
continue to change
from moment to moment

00:23:44.337 --> 00:23:47.795
but I am the only one
who seems to be aware of it.

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:53.540
Are you saying you don't
remember the last three years?

00:23:53.579 --> 00:23:56.480
You don't remember us
falling in love

00:23:56.515 --> 00:23:58.073
and getting married?

00:23:58.117 --> 00:24:00.642
I do remember
the last three years

00:24:00.686 --> 00:24:03.154
but they were different.

00:24:03.189 --> 00:24:07.626
We did not have
this relationship.

00:24:07.660 --> 00:24:09.127
We were friends.

00:24:09.161 --> 00:24:14.121
And the Enterprise did not have
a battle with the Cardassians.

00:24:17.603 --> 00:24:19.798
And no one believes me.

00:24:23.309 --> 00:24:25.277
Whatever's wrong

00:24:25.311 --> 00:24:27.438
whatever happened

00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:28.913
I want you to know

00:24:28.981 --> 00:24:31.211
that I believe you

00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:33.047
and that I love you.

00:24:33.085 --> 00:24:37.215
And together, we'll find out
what's happening.

00:24:39.458 --> 00:24:41.449
I am initiating a subspace scan

00:24:41.494 --> 00:24:43.485
to search for
temporal anomalies

00:24:43.529 --> 00:24:44.928
both on and off the ship.

00:24:45.031 --> 00:24:47.898
Counselor Troi,
please report to Sick Bay.

00:24:47.933 --> 00:24:49.457
I'm on my way.

00:24:49.502 --> 00:24:52.596
Let me know
if you find anything.

00:24:57.843 --> 00:25:03.304
Commander, how long have I been
married to Counselor Troi?

00:25:03.349 --> 00:25:06.318
Two years, one month
and 12 days.

00:25:06.352 --> 00:25:08.343
And when did this
relationship begin?

00:25:08.387 --> 00:25:10.082
It is my understanding

00:25:10.122 --> 00:25:13.888
your romantic affiliation began
shortly after you recovered

00:25:13.993 --> 00:25:16.461
from your spinal injury
on Stardate 45587.

00:25:16.495 --> 00:25:19.123
It was six months later
that you asked Commander Riker

00:25:19.165 --> 00:25:22.464
for his formal permission
to court Counselor Troi.

00:25:22.501 --> 00:25:25.664
You felt to do otherwise
would be dishonorable.

00:25:25.704 --> 00:25:27.171
And then we mated?

00:25:27.206 --> 00:25:28.639
I am not privy

00:25:28.674 --> 00:25:30.869
to the exact details
of when, where or how

00:25:30.910 --> 00:25:33.071
your first coupling took place.

00:25:33.112 --> 00:25:34.579
I could investigate it.

00:25:34.613 --> 00:25:37.343
No, that is all right.

00:25:39.285 --> 00:25:40.752
I am detecting

00:25:40.786 --> 00:25:43.254
no temporal anomalies
in this system.

00:25:43.289 --> 00:25:47.123
Perhaps we should attempt
to pinpoint the exact moment

00:25:47.159 --> 00:25:49.491
when events
became discontinuous.

00:25:49.528 --> 00:25:51.621
Do you remember
the first change?

00:25:51.664 --> 00:25:52.722
I was in Sick Bay.

00:25:52.765 --> 00:25:55.063
Dr. Crusher told me
I had a concussion

00:25:55.101 --> 00:25:57.262
but I do not remember
that happening.

00:25:57.303 --> 00:26:01.205
Think back... are you certain
that was the very first change?

00:26:01.240 --> 00:26:03.606
Before...

00:26:06.212 --> 00:26:08.737
Yes.
Yes, I was in Engineering.

00:26:08.781 --> 00:26:10.646
I felt a wave of dizziness

00:26:10.683 --> 00:26:13.550
and when I looked up,
you and Commander La Forge

00:26:13.586 --> 00:26:15.520
were on the opposite side
of the room

00:26:15.554 --> 00:26:17.283
and Captain Picard was gone.

00:26:17.323 --> 00:26:21.225
I thought I had
blacked out for a moment

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:22.989
and had not observed
your movements.

00:26:23.028 --> 00:26:28.432
And at my birthday party,
the cake was chocolate

00:26:28.467 --> 00:26:29.900
and then it was yellow.

00:26:30.002 --> 00:26:31.526
And Commander Riker told me

00:26:31.570 --> 00:26:33.697
Captain Picard
was not going to attend

00:26:33.739 --> 00:26:35.434
and then suddenly he was there.

00:26:35.474 --> 00:26:37.908
Hmm... we should try to find

00:26:37.943 --> 00:26:40.571
the commonalities
in these events.

00:26:40.613 --> 00:26:42.808
Who were the people
you were with?

00:26:42.848 --> 00:26:46.215
Everyone was
at my birthday party.

00:26:46.252 --> 00:26:49.050
Then I was with Counselor Troi

00:26:49.088 --> 00:26:52.182
then Commander La Forge
came in...

00:26:52.224 --> 00:26:53.885
Geordi...

00:26:53.926 --> 00:26:57.327
Geordi was present
at all three locations

00:26:57.363 --> 00:26:59.354
and he was near me in each case

00:26:59.398 --> 00:27:01.764
just before
I noticed the differences.

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:03.631
There has to be a connection.

00:27:03.669 --> 00:27:05.296
It is possible.

00:27:05.337 --> 00:27:09.008
We should speak
to Commander La Forge.

00:27:10.209 --> 00:27:14.908
Doctor, is Geordi well enough
to answer a few questions?

00:27:17.116 --> 00:27:19.084
Geordi's dead.

00:27:29.328 --> 00:27:32.764
There do not appear to be
any unusual readings.

00:27:32.798 --> 00:27:35.858
Energy residuals
from the plasma burns

00:27:35.901 --> 00:27:39.268
the beginnings of
cellular decomposition...

00:27:39.304 --> 00:27:42.899
I see nothing that connects
these bio-readings

00:27:42.941 --> 00:27:45.910
to your recent sense
of discontinuity.

00:27:45.944 --> 00:27:47.878
What about his VISOR?

00:27:54.186 --> 00:27:55.710
I still see nothing unusual.

00:27:55.754 --> 00:27:57.449
Perhaps we should activate it.

00:27:57.489 --> 00:28:00.549
Hook it up
to the diagnostic array

00:28:00.592 --> 00:28:02.321
and I'll check it out.

00:28:10.836 --> 00:28:12.667
The VISOR is active.

00:28:14.740 --> 00:28:16.731
Worf, are you all right?

00:28:18.744 --> 00:28:21.713
Have you noticed
another discontinuity?

00:28:24.316 --> 00:28:26.477
Dr. Crusher was not here.

00:28:26.518 --> 00:28:28.645
Dr. Ogawa was.

00:28:28.687 --> 00:28:30.484
Doctor Ogawa?

00:28:31.990 --> 00:28:34.356
And my uniform has changed.

00:28:34.393 --> 00:28:36.054
What is my rank and position?

00:28:36.095 --> 00:28:37.426
You're a Commander

00:28:37.463 --> 00:28:39.363
and First Officer.

00:28:39.398 --> 00:28:42.367
Are we still married?

00:28:42.401 --> 00:28:44.198
Yes.

00:28:44.236 --> 00:28:48.468
I am detecting a quantum flux
in your cellular RNA.

00:28:48.507 --> 00:28:50.134
What does that mean?

00:28:50.175 --> 00:28:51.802
I do not know.

00:28:51.844 --> 00:28:54.813
I will have to analyze
these readings.

00:29:00.486 --> 00:29:02.681
I have found
that the quantum flux

00:29:02.721 --> 00:29:04.518
in Worf's cellular RNA

00:29:04.556 --> 00:29:06.615
extends
to the subatomic level.

00:29:06.658 --> 00:29:09.320
It is asynchronous
with normal matter.

00:29:09.361 --> 00:29:10.692
In essence, Captain

00:29:10.729 --> 00:29:13.698
Mr. Worf does not belong
in our universe.

00:29:13.732 --> 00:29:14.699
What?

00:29:14.733 --> 00:29:16.132
All matter in the universe

00:29:16.168 --> 00:29:19.865
resonates on a quantum level
with a unique signature.

00:29:19.938 --> 00:29:21.872
That signature is constant.

00:29:21.907 --> 00:29:24.740
It cannot be changed
through any known process.

00:29:24.776 --> 00:29:27.244
It is the basic foundation
of existence.

00:29:27.279 --> 00:29:29.747
Are you saying
that Worf's quantum signature

00:29:29.781 --> 00:29:31.373
is different from ours?

00:29:31.416 --> 00:29:33.509
Yes, sir.
I cannot explain it.

00:29:33.552 --> 00:29:37.249
It is as if he originates from
a different quantum universe.

00:29:37.289 --> 00:29:40.486
Mr. Worf, you say
the discontinuities started

00:29:40.526 --> 00:29:41.891
to occur after you returned

00:29:41.927 --> 00:29:43.986
from a bat'leth tournament
on Forcas III.

00:29:44.029 --> 00:29:45.087
Yes, sir.

00:29:45.130 --> 00:29:46.893
Now, I know for a fact
that you never attended

00:29:46.999 --> 00:29:48.660
that tournament,
and that no shuttlecraft

00:29:48.700 --> 00:29:50.361
has left the Enterprise
for over a month.

00:29:50.402 --> 00:29:52.165
I understand that

00:29:52.204 --> 00:29:54.570
but I also clearly remember
attending the tournament

00:29:54.606 --> 00:29:56.631
and returning to the ship
in a shuttlecraft.

00:29:56.675 --> 00:29:58.609
Do you remember the route
you took to return?

00:29:58.644 --> 00:29:59.770
Yes.

00:29:59.811 --> 00:30:00.903
Let's backtrack that course.

00:30:01.013 --> 00:30:03.243
See if there are any
unusual readings or anomalies.

00:30:03.282 --> 00:30:04.271
Aye, sir.

00:30:08.987 --> 00:30:10.784
If I may inquire, sir

00:30:10.822 --> 00:30:13.916
how long have you been Captain
of the Enterprise?

00:30:14.026 --> 00:30:15.516
Four years.

00:30:15.561 --> 00:30:18.257
Ever since
Captain Picard was killed

00:30:18.297 --> 00:30:20.458
in the incident with the Borg.

00:30:22.834 --> 00:30:24.927
You don't remember
any of this, do you?

00:30:27.606 --> 00:30:29.233
I do remember.

00:30:29.274 --> 00:30:31.799
I just remember it differently.

00:30:40.485 --> 00:30:41.577
Captain

00:30:41.620 --> 00:30:43.281
I'm picking up a minor
subspace disturbance

00:30:43.322 --> 00:30:44.448
off the port bow.

00:30:44.489 --> 00:30:45.854
- Full stop.
- Aye, sir.

00:30:45.891 --> 00:30:47.051
Analysis, Mr. Data.

00:30:47.092 --> 00:30:48.957
It appears to be
a quantum fissure

00:30:48.994 --> 00:30:50.825
in the space-time continuum.

00:30:50.862 --> 00:30:53.262
On screen.

00:30:53.298 --> 00:30:55.357
The anomaly cannot be seen

00:30:55.400 --> 00:30:57.300
but I believe I can enhance it

00:30:57.336 --> 00:30:59.964
with a warp field
to make it visible.

00:31:01.506 --> 00:31:02.734
Is it dangerous?

00:31:02.774 --> 00:31:04.639
Not from this distance, sir.

00:31:04.676 --> 00:31:08.510
I am also detecting an ion trail
intersecting the phenomenon.

00:31:08.547 --> 00:31:10.105
I believe it was left

00:31:10.148 --> 00:31:13.276
by a Starfleet
type-6 shuttlecraft.

00:31:13.318 --> 00:31:14.910
So I was here.

00:31:14.987 --> 00:31:18.923
I have an explanation, sir.

00:31:19.024 --> 00:31:21.584
I believe the quantum
fissure we discovered

00:31:21.627 --> 00:31:24.653
is a fixed point across
the space-time continuum...

00:31:24.696 --> 00:31:29.030
a keyhole which intersects
many other quantum realities.

00:31:29.067 --> 00:31:31.558
What do you mean,
"quantum realities?"

00:31:31.603 --> 00:31:33.730
For any event, there is
an infinite number

00:31:33.772 --> 00:31:34.864
of possible outcomes.

00:31:34.906 --> 00:31:37.397
Our choices determine
which outcomes will follow

00:31:37.442 --> 00:31:41.037
but there is a theory
in quantum physics

00:31:41.079 --> 00:31:45.539
that all possibilities
that can happen, do happen

00:31:45.584 --> 00:31:47.882
in alternate quantum realities.

00:31:47.919 --> 00:31:51.480
And somehow I have been shifting
from one reality to another.

00:31:51.523 --> 00:31:53.047
That is correct.

00:31:53.091 --> 00:31:54.524
How did this happen?

00:31:56.595 --> 00:31:58.290
When Worf's shuttlecraft

00:31:58.330 --> 00:32:00.890
came into contact
with the quantum fissure

00:32:00.932 --> 00:32:03.799
I believe its warp engines
caused a small break

00:32:03.835 --> 00:32:06.497
in the barriers
between quantum realities.

00:32:06.538 --> 00:32:09.837
Worf was thrown
into a state of quantum flux.

00:32:09.875 --> 00:32:11.843
He immediately shifted
into other realities.

00:32:11.877 --> 00:32:14.903
And Geordi's VISOR
somehow triggered that effect.

00:32:15.013 --> 00:32:16.480
Exactly.

00:32:16.515 --> 00:32:18.847
The VISOR uses
a subspace field pulse.

00:32:18.884 --> 00:32:21.045
I believe that whenever Geordi
came near Worf

00:32:21.086 --> 00:32:23.816
the field pulse intensified
the quantum flux

00:32:23.855 --> 00:32:27.154
and pushed Worf
into another reality.

00:32:27.192 --> 00:32:29.251
Well, how can we find
my original quantum state

00:32:29.294 --> 00:32:30.261
and return me too it?

00:32:30.295 --> 00:32:32.627
We could scan
the quantum fissure

00:32:32.664 --> 00:32:34.928
using a subspace
differential pulse.

00:32:34.966 --> 00:32:37.298
Maybe we could find
the quantum state

00:32:37.336 --> 00:32:39.167
that shares Worf's signature

00:32:39.204 --> 00:32:41.172
and find a way to get him back.

00:32:41.206 --> 00:32:43.436
An excellent idea, Lieutenant.

00:33:00.359 --> 00:33:03.385
Worf...

00:33:03.428 --> 00:33:05.623
from what I understand

00:33:05.664 --> 00:33:10.067
there's a good chance
my Worf won't return.

00:33:10.102 --> 00:33:12.400
I guess it's just hard
for me to accept

00:33:12.437 --> 00:33:20.139
that there's a reality out there
where you never loved me.

00:33:22.381 --> 00:33:28.411
Deanna, I have always
considered you a close friend.

00:33:28.453 --> 00:33:30.921
And although I have never

00:33:30.989 --> 00:33:35.153
seriously considered
a romantic relationship

00:33:35.193 --> 00:33:39.254
I would not be opposed
to the possibility.

00:33:39.297 --> 00:33:41.857
What about our children?

00:33:43.268 --> 00:33:44.929
Children?

00:33:44.970 --> 00:33:46.460
You didn't know?

00:33:48.206 --> 00:33:51.369
When the last shift
occurred in Sick Bay

00:33:51.410 --> 00:33:53.776
we did not have any children.

00:33:59.317 --> 00:34:01.808
We have a little girl,
Shannara.

00:34:01.853 --> 00:34:03.320
She's two years old.

00:34:03.355 --> 00:34:07.815
And a three-year-old boy,
Eric-Christopher.

00:34:12.731 --> 00:34:14.665
What about Alexander?

00:34:14.699 --> 00:34:16.963
Alexander?

00:34:21.173 --> 00:34:24.734
He was my son
in another reality.

00:34:41.460 --> 00:34:42.927
I've used a differential pulse

00:34:42.961 --> 00:34:45.020
to analyze
over 10 million quantum states

00:34:45.063 --> 00:34:46.155
within the fissure

00:34:46.198 --> 00:34:48.462
but I still haven't found
one with your signature.

00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:50.195
This may take some time, sir.

00:34:52.370 --> 00:34:53.894
Captain, a Bajoran ship
is approaching.

00:34:53.939 --> 00:34:54.906
Red Alert.

00:34:54.940 --> 00:34:56.237
The Bajorans?

00:34:56.274 --> 00:34:57.571
Ever since the Bajorans

00:34:57.609 --> 00:34:59.270
overpowered
the Cardassian Empire

00:34:59.311 --> 00:35:01.245
they've become
more and more aggressive.

00:35:01.279 --> 00:35:03.713
Yesterday, they destroyed
one of our subspace telescopes

00:35:03.748 --> 00:35:06.649
because they thought we were
using it to spy against them.

00:35:06.685 --> 00:35:08.016
They're charging
their weapons, sir.

00:35:08.053 --> 00:35:10.180
Shields!

00:35:10.222 --> 00:35:12.087
Return fire.

00:35:12.123 --> 00:35:13.988
They've damaged
our power systems, sir.

00:35:14.025 --> 00:35:16.994
It's caused an energy surge
within the subspace pulse.

00:35:17.028 --> 00:35:19.519
The quantum fissure
is beginning to destabilize.

00:35:19.564 --> 00:35:21.623
Can we disengage the pulse?

00:35:24.302 --> 00:35:25.735
Too late, sir.

00:35:31.643 --> 00:35:33.133
What the hell is happening?

00:35:33.178 --> 00:35:35.908
The barriers between quantum
realities are breaking down.

00:35:35.947 --> 00:35:39.747
Other realities
are emerging into our own.

00:35:55.233 --> 00:35:58.066
The Bajoran ship
is disengaging, sir.

00:35:58.102 --> 00:36:01.503
The rate of quantum incursions
is increasing exponentially.

00:36:01.539 --> 00:36:03.700
At this rate, the sector
will be completely filled

00:36:03.741 --> 00:36:06.005
with Enterprises
within three days.

00:36:06.044 --> 00:36:09.673
Captain, we're receiving
285,000 hails.

00:36:09.714 --> 00:36:12.239
I wish I knew what to tell them.

00:36:12.283 --> 00:36:15.411
Mr. Data, can we stop
these incursions?

00:36:15.453 --> 00:36:17.683
Perhaps.
If we can find the ship

00:36:17.722 --> 00:36:20.714
that matches Commander Worf's
quantum signature.

00:36:20.758 --> 00:36:22.453
How would that help?

00:36:22.493 --> 00:36:25.894
It was Worf's shuttlecraft
which traversed the fissure

00:36:25.963 --> 00:36:28.488
and weakened the barriers
between quantum realities.

00:36:28.533 --> 00:36:31.366
If he reenters the fissure
in his original shuttle

00:36:31.402 --> 00:36:33.632
and emits
a broad-spectrum warp field

00:36:33.671 --> 00:36:35.229
it may be enough
to seal the fissure

00:36:35.273 --> 00:36:38.106
and stop additional realities
from entering our own.

00:36:38.142 --> 00:36:39.302
What then?

00:36:39.344 --> 00:36:40.709
How do we get the Enterprises

00:36:40.745 --> 00:36:42.906
that are already here
back to where they belong?

00:36:42.947 --> 00:36:45.541
In theory,
the act of sealing the fissure

00:36:45.583 --> 00:36:49.679
should restore the barriers
between quantum states.

00:36:49.721 --> 00:36:52.918
The ships would return
to their own realities.

00:36:53.024 --> 00:36:58.155
Lieutenant Crusher,
send a general hail... all ships.

00:36:58.196 --> 00:37:01.131
Aye, sir.

00:37:01.165 --> 00:37:03.861
This is Captain Riker
of the Enterprise.

00:37:03.901 --> 00:37:05.869
That is, the Enterprise

00:37:05.970 --> 00:37:08.461
that is indigenous
to this universe.

00:37:08.506 --> 00:37:11.703
We've all encountered
a quantum anomaly.

00:37:11.743 --> 00:37:13.677
We think we have found a way

00:37:13.711 --> 00:37:16.043
to return us all
to our proper realities

00:37:16.080 --> 00:37:17.877
but we need to find that ship

00:37:17.915 --> 00:37:21.078
which exhibits
a certain quantum signature.

00:37:21.119 --> 00:37:24.748
Our Mr. Data will transmit
that signature to you now.

00:37:31.929 --> 00:37:33.396
Anything?

00:37:33.431 --> 00:37:35.296
There's too much com traffic,
sir.

00:37:35.333 --> 00:37:38.097
It's tough to isolate
who's talking to who.

00:37:38.136 --> 00:37:39.569
Wait a minute.

00:37:39.604 --> 00:37:40.866
Here it is.

00:37:40.905 --> 00:37:42.463
Someone's responding.

00:37:42.507 --> 00:37:43.735
On screen.

00:37:45.376 --> 00:37:47.310
Captain, it would appear
that we have found

00:37:47.345 --> 00:37:49.245
the quantum signature
you were looking for.

00:37:49.280 --> 00:37:50.645
Data believes

00:37:50.681 --> 00:37:53.241
that by sending Worf back
through the fissure again

00:37:53.284 --> 00:37:56.378
it would return us all
to our proper realities.

00:37:56.421 --> 00:37:58.480
Our Data has said
the same thing.

00:37:58.523 --> 00:38:01.686
We need you to send us
your Shuttlecraft Curie.

00:38:01.726 --> 00:38:03.387
We're launching it now.

00:38:03.428 --> 00:38:04.622
Thank you.

00:38:04.662 --> 00:38:07.529
It's good
to see you again, Captain.

00:38:07.565 --> 00:38:09.396
It's been a long time.

00:38:16.607 --> 00:38:18.040
Did they send the right shuttle?

00:38:18.075 --> 00:38:20.737
Yes, sir.
It matches Commander Worf's

00:38:20.778 --> 00:38:22.769
quantum signature precisely.

00:38:22.814 --> 00:38:25.408
I have remodulated
the shuttle's engines

00:38:25.450 --> 00:38:27.281
to emit an inverse warp field.

00:38:27.318 --> 00:38:28.979
You will need to activate
that field

00:38:29.020 --> 00:38:30.817
at the precise moment
you enter the fissure.

00:38:30.855 --> 00:38:31.879
Assuming it works

00:38:31.923 --> 00:38:34.016
will I find myself
near my own ship?

00:38:34.058 --> 00:38:35.685
That is one possibility.

00:38:35.726 --> 00:38:37.353
However,
the uncertainty principle

00:38:37.395 --> 00:38:40.330
dictates that time is a variable
in this equation.

00:38:40.364 --> 00:38:41.831
You may end up

00:38:41.866 --> 00:38:44.835
several days before the event
or several days after.

00:38:44.869 --> 00:38:46.894
There is no way to tell.

00:38:46.971 --> 00:38:48.529
I understand.

00:38:48.573 --> 00:38:50.541
Good luck.

00:39:37.889 --> 00:39:39.880
Setting course for the fissure.

00:39:39.924 --> 00:39:40.913
Acknowledged.

00:39:42.260 --> 00:39:44.888
Captain, the shuttlecraft
is under attack.

00:39:44.929 --> 00:39:46.453
The Bajorans again.

00:39:46.497 --> 00:39:48.897
No, sir.
It's one of the Enterprises.

00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:51.468
They're hailing us.

00:39:51.502 --> 00:39:53.800
On screen.

00:39:53.838 --> 00:39:56.432
We won't go back.

00:39:56.474 --> 00:39:58.499
You don't know what it's like
in our universe.

00:39:58.543 --> 00:40:00.170
The Federation's gone!

00:40:00.211 --> 00:40:02.702
The Borg is everywhere!

00:40:02.747 --> 00:40:04.715
We're one
of the last ships left.

00:40:04.749 --> 00:40:06.842
Please, you've got to help us!

00:40:06.884 --> 00:40:08.909
I'm sorry, there's no choice.

00:40:08.953 --> 00:40:11.387
If this works,
everything will return...

00:40:11.422 --> 00:40:13.117
No! We won't go back!

00:40:13.157 --> 00:40:15.751
Sir, they're firing
on the shuttlecraft.

00:40:15.793 --> 00:40:18.125
Open fire.
Try to disable them.

00:40:20.831 --> 00:40:21.923
Direct hit.

00:40:21.966 --> 00:40:23.934
Their shields have collapsed.

00:40:24.001 --> 00:40:25.730
Their engine core's
overloading.

00:40:29.307 --> 00:40:30.501
What happened?

00:40:30.541 --> 00:40:31.667
It looks like

00:40:31.709 --> 00:40:33.802
the ship had already
taken heavy damage.

00:40:33.844 --> 00:40:36.438
Their warp containment field
must have been weak.

00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:38.641
Probably from fighting
with the Borg.

00:40:38.683 --> 00:40:40.878
Captain,
Worf is entering the fissure.

00:40:43.754 --> 00:40:47.087
Charging primary systems.

00:40:47.124 --> 00:40:50.651
Initiating inverse warp field.

00:41:25.596 --> 00:41:27.154
Worf to Enterprise.

00:41:27.198 --> 00:41:28.927
Enterprise here.

00:41:29.033 --> 00:41:31.934
Captain,
is everything all right?

00:41:32.003 --> 00:41:35.666
Yes, Lieutenant.
Is there a problem?

00:41:35.706 --> 00:41:37.503
No, I do not believe so

00:41:37.541 --> 00:41:39.839
but I will explain
when I arrive.

00:41:39.877 --> 00:41:43.506
How was
the bat'leth tournament?

00:41:45.583 --> 00:41:47.210
It was fine, sir.

00:41:49.820 --> 00:41:52.516
I won Champion Standing.

00:41:59.163 --> 00:42:00.562
So, you think
this quantum fissure

00:42:00.598 --> 00:42:02.225
is nothing
that we need to worry about?

00:42:02.266 --> 00:42:03.290
No, no, I believe

00:42:03.334 --> 00:42:05.529
the inverse warp field
resealed it.

00:42:05.569 --> 00:42:07.764
I'm looking forward
to reading your report.

00:42:16.547 --> 00:42:18.276
Something wrong?

00:42:18.315 --> 00:42:20.647
I know what you
are planning, sir.

00:42:20.685 --> 00:42:22.414
I will not be surprised.

00:42:22.453 --> 00:42:24.819
Surprised? I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:42:24.855 --> 00:42:26.880
Of course you don't.

00:42:45.576 --> 00:42:46.873
Welcome home, Worf.

00:42:46.911 --> 00:42:49.471
I hope you don't mind
I let myself in.

00:42:49.513 --> 00:42:50.946
I promised Alexander

00:42:51.048 --> 00:42:53.209
I'd feed his Dalvan
hissing beetle

00:42:53.250 --> 00:42:55.650
while you were both away.

00:42:57.221 --> 00:42:59.485
So, you do not live here.

00:42:59.523 --> 00:43:02.151
What's that supposed to mean?

00:43:03.928 --> 00:43:05.828
It is a long story.

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:12.298
Happy birthday, Worf.

00:43:12.336 --> 00:43:16.636
Will wanted to give you
a surprise party, but I knew

00:43:16.674 --> 00:43:19.268
you'd hate it,
so I talked him out of it.

00:43:19.310 --> 00:43:20.777
Thank you.

00:43:20.811 --> 00:43:24.178
I know Klingons like to be alone
on their birthdays.

00:43:24.215 --> 00:43:26.513
You probably want to meditate

00:43:26.550 --> 00:43:29.280
or hit yourself
with a painstik or something.

00:43:29.320 --> 00:43:31.015
Deanna...

00:43:32.923 --> 00:43:35.050
you do not have to leave.

00:43:35.092 --> 00:43:36.525
Oh?

00:43:36.560 --> 00:43:39.222
I... have not had dinner.

00:43:39.263 --> 00:43:42.460
Would you care to join me?

00:43:42.500 --> 00:43:45.298
I'd love to.

00:44:04.221 --> 00:44:06.189
Champagne.
